<h2>Asobi 0.2 (build 372)</h2>
<p><b>Walk your compares shot to shot — no re-picking.</b></p>
<ul>
<li>Mark playlist rows as the A side and B side of a compare walk (the new A/B chips on each row, numbered in marking order), then press <b>,</b> and <b>.</b> to jump pair to pair — the playhead moves to each A, its B loads, and your compare mode and wipe stay exactly as set.</li>
<li>With nothing marked, the walk uses your version groups automatically — a playlist of grouped versions compares A/B-to-A/B out of the box. Ad-hoc compare is unchanged.</li>
<li>Browser seats walk the same pairs with the same keys; the whole room follows.</li>
<li>The expert manual, cheat sheet and web guide document the walk.</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
